   "resumo_en": "Lavô Tá Novo (transl. Washed and It Is New) is the second album by the Brazilian hardcore punk band Raimundos. It was released in 1995 through Warner Music, and its producer was Mark Dearnley, who had already worked with AC/DC, Black Sabbath and Def Leppard previously. The album was certified platinum. This album sold around five hundred thousand copies."
