   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%B3_no_Forevis",
   "resumo_en": "Só no Forevis (transl. Only in the Butt) is the fourth studio album by Brazilian hard rock band Raimundos, launched in 1999. Its title makes a reference to the word forevis, used as a euphemism to buttocks, by Brazilian humorist Mussum from the Os Trapalhões troupe of comedians.\nAt 850 thousand copies sold, it is Raimundos' best selling album.\nIt was also the last studio album with vocalist Rodolfo Abrantes."
