   "resumo_en": "Éramos 4 (transl. We Were 4, a pun on Éramos Seis) is the seventh album of the Brazilian band Raimundos. It was launched in 2001, after the exit of the founding singer Rodolfo Abrantes. The disc contains basically cover songs of Ramones, played live with Marky Ramone, ex-drummer of the Ramones."
